  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Lucy's Treats sells three different boxes of raisins: \n\n- Box $A$ contains $12$ ounces, and costs $$2.28\\,.$\n\n- Box $B$ contains $32$ ounces,  and costs $$5.44\\,.$\n\n- Box $C$ contains $22$ ounces, and costs $$3.52\\,.$\n\nWhich box of raisins is the best deal?",
  "worked_solution": "The best deal is the box with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three boxes. To compute the unit price, we divide the price by the total number of ounces.   \n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in box $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n2.28÷12=0.19\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $A$ is $$0.19.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in box $B,$ we get\n\n$$\n5.44÷32=0.17\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $B$ is $$0.17.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in box $C,$ we get\n\n$$\n3.52÷22=0.16\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $C$ is $$0.16.$\n\nFrom the above, we see that box $C$ has the lowest unit price of $$0.16/\\text{oz}.$ Therefore, box $C$ offers the best deal.",
